## Integration Tests

### Repository Adapters

Test against **real database** (use testcontainers or similar).

```java
// Repository adapter test - real DB
import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.*;

class MongoOrderRepositoryTest {

    @Test
    void persistsAndRetrievesAnOrder() {
        MongoOrderRepository repository = new MongoOrderRepository(testDbConnection);
        Order order = Order.create(Id.generate());

        repository.save(order);
        Order retrieved = repository.findById(order.getId());

        assertNotNull(retrieved);
        assertTrue(retrieved.getId().equals(order.getId()));
    }
}
```

### Application Port Adapters

Test against **real external services** (sandbox/test environment). No mocks here.

```java
// Application port adapter test - real service sandbox
import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.*;

class StripePaymentAdapterTest {

    @Test
    void chargesPaymentInTestMode() {
        StripePaymentAdapter adapter = new StripePaymentAdapter(stripeTestClient);

        PaymentResult result = adapter.charge(Money.create(100, "EUR"), "tok_visa");

        assertTrue(result.isSuccess());
    }
}
```

